# EmailJS — frontend-only email delivery for the contact form.
# 1. Create a free account at https://www.emailjs.com
# 2. Add an email service (Gmail works with vijay31235@gmail.com)
# 3. Create a template. The form sends all of these variables, so either
#    naming style works:
#      {{name}} {{email}} {{title}} {{message}} {{time}}          <- EmailJS defaults
#      {{from_name}} {{from_email}} {{reply_to}} {{subject}}      <- aliases
#    Set the template's "To Email" to vijay31235@gmail.com and "Reply To" to {{email}}.
# 4. Copy this file to `.env` and paste your ids below, then restart `npm run dev`.
#
# Until these are filled in, the form falls back to opening the visitor's mail app.

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
